# Complex number: a real and an imaginary part, both floats. Pure float math, identical on every backend. The combiners are named `plus` / `minus` / `times` because `add` / `subtract` / `multiply` are the number arithmetic primitives. Read the parts directly as `value/real` and `value/imaginary`.

load @term/seed/code/float
  find square-root

form complex
  link real, like decimal
  link imaginary, like decimal

  # (a + bi) + (c + di) = (a + c) + (b + d)i
  task plus
    take self
    take other, like complex
    like complex
    send back
      make complex
        bind real
          call add
            read self/real
            read other/real
        bind imaginary
          call add
            read self/imaginary
            read other/imaginary

  # (a + bi) - (c + di) = (a - c) + (b - d)i
  task minus
    take self
    take other, like complex
    like complex
    send back
      make complex
        bind real
          call subtract
            read self/real
            read other/real
        bind imaginary
          call subtract
            read self/imaginary
            read other/imaginary

  # (a + bi)(c + di) = (ac - bd) + (ad + bc)i
  task times
    take self
    take other, like complex
    like complex
    send back
      make complex
        bind real
          call subtract
            call multiply
              read self/real
              read other/real
            call multiply
              read self/imaginary
              read other/imaginary
        bind imaginary
          call add
            call multiply
              read self/real
              read other/imaginary
            call multiply
              read self/imaginary
              read other/real

  # the complex conjugate: negate the imaginary part
  task conjugate
    take self
    like complex
    send back
      make complex
        bind real, read self/real
        bind imaginary
          call subtract
            0.0
            read self/imaginary

  # the modulus: square-root of (real^2 + imaginary^2)
  task magnitude
    take self
    like decimal
    send back
      call square-root
        call add
          call multiply
            read self/real
            read self/real
          call multiply
            read self/imaginary
            read self/imaginary

task make-complex
  take real, like decimal
  take imaginary, like decimal
  like complex
  send back
    make complex
      bind real, read real
      bind imaginary, read imaginary
